  "developmentChecks": [
    "Confirmed early returns both at safe initialization and after primary feasibility; previous tests incorrectly required skipping the CLF stage. Corrected those assertions and added positive-CLF exact-successor and expired-budget cases.",
    "A prototype restoring CLF while retaining the full-horizon tracking objective repeatedly exhausted the 5 s budget in two short cases. That exploratory run was interrupted and is not final validation. The final secondary objective restores the original horizon tracking term after an intermediate CLF-only variant produced 74.024 m final lateral error.",
    "Replaced the tangent plane of the quadratic first-step CLF with its exact second-order-cone representation on the affine error. Nonlinear rollout admission and CLF comparison remain mandatory.",
    "Intermediate 40-hold head-on/crossing smoke runs completed, but the first full campaign exposed severe CLF scaling and saturated-seed behavior: 8 m/s brakingLead completed safely with 84.333 m final lateral error and 54 incomplete CLF stages. That campaign was interrupted and is not final success evidence.",
    "Scaled rho by max(1,rho_anchor) and the entire secondary objective by its positive anchor cost, preserving exact ordering. All six isolated secondary probes then returned normal optimal solver flags. Inverted the existing Fiala adhesion force fraction to replace the kinematic seed steering preference; optimization constraints remain unchanged.",
    "Restored the original horizon tracking term after the CLF-only campaign produced excessive final path error. Replaced the three trial scales by geometric backtracking up to twenty halvings under the same budget; feasible anchors no longer trigger repeated endpoint shooting, while infeasible restoration still can. The complete 15 m/s crossing probe retained safety with 18.987 m final lateral error and 0.876963 s maximum running time.",
    "After the seed improvement, the old 24 m primary-restoration test seed became feasible. Its 22 m variant still requires primary restoration and covers the same two-stage behavior. Two closer exploratory variants at 20 and 18 m failed to produce a feasible continuation within 20 s; they are outside the fourteen unchanged campaign fixtures and do not establish physical impossibility."
